@startuml
!define REGISTER_WIDTH 8

rectangle "Software Reset Register (Offset 02Fh)" {
  
  package "Bit Layout" {
    rectangle "D07-D03\nRsvd" as rsvd #lightgray
    rectangle "D02\nSoftware Reset For\nDAT Line" as dat
    rectangle "D01\nSoftware Reset For\nCMD Line" as cmd
    rectangle "D00\nSoftware Reset For\nAll" as all
  }
  
  rsvd -right- dat
  dat -right- cmd
  cmd -right- all
}

note right of dat
  **Software Reset For DAT Line (RWAC)**
  Only part of data circuit is reset.
  DMA circuit is also reset.
  
  **Cleared registers/bits:**
  • Buffer Data Port register
  • Present State register bits:
    - Buffer Read Enable
    - Buffer Write Enable
    - Read Transfer Active
    - Write Transfer Active
    - DAT Line Active
    - Command Inhibit (DAT)
  • Block Gap Control register bits:
    - Continue Request
    - Stop At Block Gap Request
  • Normal Interrupt Status register bits:
    - Buffer Read Ready
    - Buffer Write Ready
    - DMA Interrupt
    - Block Gap Event
    - Transfer Complete
  
  **Values:**
  1 = Reset
  0 = Work
end note

note right of rsvd
  Location: 07-03
  Attribute: Rsvd
  Reserved
end note

@enduml